        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This feature seems to be more useful and effective for upcoming new limitation based on estimated memory usage (uncompressed size) [^1].\n\nThat number, in my opinion, is meant to be applied for remote players. So local-only objects should be markable as \"not intended to propagate onto remote environments\".\n\n[^1]: https://ask.vrchat.com/t/developer-update-14-march-2024/23401",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-26T10:32:20.266Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Avatars may contain GameObjects that are used only locally. For example, camera extensions and inventory systems based on Avatar Dynamics. I think that they should be excluded from performance rank calculation if they are always disabled in remote environments.\nI know that it is hard to determine which objects are local by inspecting animator controllers. My proposal is based on explicitly marking and runtime content modification to avoid animator inspection.\n- Mark local objects as \"local only\" by tag or custom component.\n- Remove marked objects while loading avatars as with camera components in avatars used by non-friends.\nThis feature makes the performance rank system more accurate and reasonable. It will help to motivate developers to optimize their avatars.",
